@startuml sdd-04b_order_flow_sequence
title SDD-04b — One tick becomes one order, DETAIL (UML **sequence diagram**)\nThe cross-module path call by call, and the symbol lease refusing a manual order.\nThe same path in six messages is SDD-04a — read that first.
autonumber
participant "market_data\n(market websocket)" as MD
participant "Event bus" as Bus
participant "strategy\nMarketTickEventHandler → LiveTradingCoordinator" as ST
participant "trading\nIOrderSubmission (impl)" as TRs
participant "trading\nITradingSession (impl)" as TRt
participant "binance_gateway\nITradingSessionFactory" as GW
participant "Binance Futures" as BN
participant "trading\nuser-data stream → Feed" as UDS
participant "surfaces\n(positions card)" as UI

== arm (once) ==
ST -> TRt : claim_symbol("BTCUSDT", owner="strategy")
note right of TRt : trading records the lease;\nit does not know what "strategy" is

== every closed candle ==
MD -> Bus : MarketTickEvent
Bus -> ST : (subscribed in strategy.subscribe())
ST -> ST : StrategyEngine.on_candle() → Signal
ST -> TRs : preview(OrderIntent)  → OrderPreview
ST -> TRs : execute(OrderIntent)
TRs -> TRt : session enabled? limits? lease ok for owner?
TRs -> GW : create_trading_client()
GW -> BN : POST /fapi/v1/order
BN --> TRs : order accepted
BN -> UDS : ORDER_TRADE_UPDATE / ACCOUNT_UPDATE
UDS -> Bus : OrderFilledEvent · PositionChangedEvent
Bus -> UI : (via QtEventBridge, trading's feed)

== manual order from Dev Board on the same symbol ==
UI -> TRs : execute(OrderIntent(owner="manual"))
TRs -> TRt : lease held by another owner?
TRt --> TRs : yes → refuse (SYMBOL_LEASED)
note over TRs, TRt : EPIC-024B §4.1.2's hard block, expressed without trading knowing strategy
@enduml
